 BEYOND THE MAIN SEED
 Weak RNG also hit paper-wallet keys, clone / Key Teleport material, and some Secure Notes passwords — even when the BIP-39 seed itself came from dice (WizardSardine / Block).
 LOWER RISK
-At least 50 private dice rolls at seed creation. A long truly random BIP-39 passphrase (not the device PIN) may buy time, but weak passphrases are not enough — BTC Sessions reported a confirmed Mk3 drain with a two-word passphrase; ColeTU saw 1–3 BIP39-word passphrases on a compromised Mk3 seed swept in ~6–7 days. CK tripwire is mapping live how far added dice/passphrase entropy currently stops sweeps (zero-entropy control swept in ~1h; frontier ~11 bits by Aug 12 after a low/pass honeypot sweep; mid/high bands still live). Still migrate when practical.
